  {"id":124,"x":360,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Shell Shrine","descriptions":["Long, curving protrusions jut out from between the shells that make up the walls here, wickedly sharp and waiting for someone careless enough to stumble over the simple altar nestled in the sand floor.  Dark husks of now dead malchata stand a quiet vigil in the recesses opposite the shrine entrance, their bodies somehow preserved from reverting back into sand."],"exits":[{"to":40,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00"},
